# Who owns what in OpenADLC itself. This mirrors AGENTS.md's `## Human
# review` section, path for path, so GitHub's code-owner rule and the bridge ask
# for the same approval: the files that define how the crew is held in check.
# Every other path has no code owner and is left to the crew's review. Change
# the two together. (An organization alone is not an owner GitHub accepts; it
# takes a user or an `@org/team`.)
/config/                              @orzelig
/infra/                               @orzelig
/.github/workflows/                   @orzelig
/.github/scripts/scope-check.mjs      @orzelig
/docs/platform-plan.md                @orzelig
/apps/bridge/src/automation.ts        @orzelig
/apps/bridge/src/merge-line.ts        @orzelig
/apps/bridge/src/gates.ts             @orzelig
/packages/shared/src/access.ts        @orzelig
/packages/shared/src/authorship.ts    @orzelig
/packages/shared/src/human-review.ts  @orzelig
/packages/shared/src/checks.ts        @orzelig
/crew/skills/*/tools.yaml             @orzelig
